# The conformance suite IS the specification (packages/core/test/CONFORMANCE.md:
# "a test change is a spec change and needs the same review as a roadmap edit").
#
# Nothing enforced that. There was no CODEOWNERS, no CI step referencing CONFORMANCE.md,
# and no count or hash assertion — so an agent or a hurried human could delete a pin
# during a refactor and the build stayed green. The claim "the suite is the spec" is only
# as strong as the thing that stops the suite being edited to fit the code.
#
# Replace @OWNER with the real owner (a GitHub handle or team) for this to take effect.
/packages/core/test/            @OWNER
/packages/core/test/CONFORMANCE.md  @OWNER
/product-thesis.md              @OWNER
/product-roadmap.md             @OWNER
